<title>FRANCE: French stocks slightly weaker on profit-taking.</title>
<headline>French stocks slightly weaker on profit-taking.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-07-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>French shares slightly lower at midday on Thursday after giving back early surge that lifted the CAC index above 3,000 for the first time.</p>
<p>* CAC-40 down 4.26 points or 0.14 percent at 2,983.75</p>
<p>* CAC-40 July futures down 14 at 2,985</p>
<p>* Valeo falls 1.97 percent to 404 francs on profit-taking on strong recent gains</p>
<p>* SGS-Thomson falls 1.07 percent on lower first-half results.</p>
</text>
